1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
An exam form is stuck.
Who can the student ask?

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Time goes into finding the right department.
The same question gets asked again.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,000
The student cannot tell
where the query stands.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,000
A language barrier adds to the difficulty.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,000
The right help arrives late.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,300
This is the AI-Powered Student Support
& Query Management System.

7
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:30,500
From students to the principal,
everyone connects on one platform.

8
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:36,000
This demo uses mock services
matching the planned API structure.

9
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,000
One clear route to support.

10
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Aarav is an ITI student.

11
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,000
After registration, he logs in.

12
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:50,000
His dashboard shows his queries
and their current status.

13
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,000
FAQ search gives him general information.

14
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:58,000
He opens the chatbot for help
in his own language.

15
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Aarav asks in Gujarati:
“How do I apply for a scholarship?”

16
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,000
The AI identifies his language
and the subject of the query.

17
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:13,000
It finds a relevant answer
in approved FAQs.

18
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:16,500
This demo shows guidance
on the application process.

19
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:19,000
The source of the answer is visible.

20
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Clear information reduces
the need to ask repeatedly.

21
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Aarav describes an examination
registration error in Hindi.

22
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:33,000
The AI classifies it
as an examination-related query.

23
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:37,000
But it finds no verified answer
for this specific issue.

24
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Instead of guessing,
it asks for the details it needs.

25
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Aarav shares his registration number
and the error he sees.

26
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:50,000
He is then asked for permission
to create a ticket.

27
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:54,000
After consent, the ticket is routed
to the Examination department.

28
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Rule-based assignment identifies
the responsible staff member.

29
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Aarav now knows who to contact.

30
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:09,500
The Examination staff member receives
the ticket on their dashboard.

31
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:13,000
The student's details arrive with the ticket.

32
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:16,500
The student does not need
to explain everything again.

33
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:22,000
The staff member works on the query
and sends a reply.

34
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:27,500
In this example, they explain the correction
and mark the ticket resolved.

35
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:33,000
If another department is needed,
the ticket can be forwarded.

36
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:39,000
A reply notification prompts Aarav
to open the ticket timeline.

37
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:43,500
He can see every stage
and the responsible staff member's actions.

38
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:48,000
He reviews the reply,
then gives a rating and feedback.

39
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:53,000
His experience can help
improve future support.

40
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,200
The administrator reviews a staff-suggested FAQ.

41
00:02:58,200 --> 00:03:04,000
It is published after reviewing
the Gujarati, Hindi and English text.

42
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:09,300
The useful answer becomes available
to other students.

43
00:03:09,300 --> 00:03:12,800
The administrator manages
users, departments and rules.

44
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:18,000
AI logs show every action,
from answer retrieval to ticket creation.

45
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:25,600
The principal sees department performance,
response times and pending tickets.

46
00:03:25,600 --> 00:03:29,700
We advance the demo clock
to demonstrate escalation.

47
00:03:29,700 --> 00:03:37,400
Proposed: supervisor notice at 24 hours;
principal/admin escalation at 48 hours.

48
00:03:37,400 --> 00:03:40,000
The institute can change these thresholds.

49
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:43,000
Responsibility can be reassigned when needed.

50
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:49,100
Planned: React and Material UI
will power the website.

51
00:03:49,100 --> 00:03:53,800
Laravel 12 REST APIs will manage tickets
and check permissions.

52
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:56,400
MySQL will be the single source of truth.

53
00:03:56,400 --> 00:04:01,100
Python FastAPI and Google Gemini
will provide the AI service.

54
00:04:01,100 --> 00:04:03,700
AI will not modify the database directly.

55
00:04:03,700 --> 00:04:07,900
It will send requests only through
authenticated Laravel APIs.

56
00:04:07,900 --> 00:04:10,000
Each AI action will be logged.

57
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:13,000
Deployment on an Ubuntu server is planned.

58
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:20,100
Students get a clear path
from a question to an answer.

59
00:04:20,100 --> 00:04:24,200
Department ownership and progress
become easier to see.

60
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:29,300
Future expansion: WhatsApp, a mobile app,
and voice-based assistance.

61
00:04:29,300 --> 00:04:33,900
More ITIs could be connected
through a Gujarat-wide platform.

62
00:04:33,900 --> 00:04:38,000
Deeper analytics can help guide
service-improvement decisions.

63
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:46,200
Our goal is timely, appropriate support
for every ITI student.

64
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:52,300
Transparent work and accountable departments:
a clear direction for student-centred service.

65
00:04:52,300 --> 00:05:00,000
One Website. One Intelligent Support Agent.
One Centralized Student Support System.
